notes               = "Untitled in source. Turns on وقت: love 'does not want time', and then هیچ وقت نداریم, which is at once 'we have no time' and 'we never do'. English can only hold one at a time; the lantern takes the first and lets 'always' in the last line do the other. 11 Tir = 1 July 1996. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben. Photo check 2026-07-31 (p168): the page prints با همیم — the doubled م (هممیم) was a transcription slip, corrected to match the page."
draft               = true

===persian===

کوچک‌ترین پرنده به من آموخت...
دوست داشتن وقت نمی‌خواهد...
من و تو...
هیچ وقت نداریم...
و... همیشه با همیم...
۱۳۷۵/۴/۱۱

===machine===

The smallest bird taught me...
loving does not ask for time...
You and I...
have no time at all...
and... we are together always...
1375/4/11

===lantern===

The smallest bird taught me
that loving does not ask for time.
You and I
have no time at all —
and we are together always...

1375/4/11

===translation===

===footnotes===

هیچ وقت نداریم means both *we have no time* and *we never do*, and the poem needs both at
once: the lovers are given nothing and it turns out to be enough.
